\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 The Great Western Goat Track had been designed by someone who understood neither goats nor tracks,  much less the dimensions of limos. That night, a convoy of twenty-three stately white Lincoln Continentals picked its way over crests that could have delivered them to thin air, and hairpins that could have rolled them into gullies a Sherpa might not have climbed out of.\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 The conditions of the Lincolns ranged from fastidiously maintained to held together by sequins and showmanship. Blue lights flashed from the roofs of the hardtops. Some convertibles had soft-tops that could have been made from second-hand ponchos; their rhinestones twinkled in the moonlight like a V-8 powered star system.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 From the lead car, a siren wailed the tune of \'93Ground Hog\'94 in H
\f2\fs18 \super \'81\'f3
\f1\fs22 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \nosupersub . In the backseat, two Tulsa \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
McLeans were trying to sing along in West German but couldn\'92t cram all the syllables in. In the shotgun seat, another Tulsa twiddled the dial on a police radio and found only static.\
Chanta rode in the back seat with the pair of singing Tulsas, clutching the door handle as the driver\'97a Speedway series predictably named Steve Grayson\'97threw the soft-suspension limo around like it was a Dodge Charger built for the track. \'93Is the siren really necessary?\'94 Chanta complained.\
Through the mountain mist, a mansion appeared\'97three stories of architectural arrogance squatting behind gates that probably cost more than most people\'92s education. A plaque thanked the accountant and lawyers who had made the owner liquid enough to build it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 With a chorus of crunching gravel, the cars surrounded the gate and lurched to a halt. Doors and boots sprang open. Hollow-body Gibsons and upright basses appeared to jump from the cars with Elvi arms attached. Battered tweed amps followed with heavier effort, as did a generator. Cables uncoiled across the driveway. The generator coughed into life and amps hummed. One Elvis counted one\'85two\'85one\'97two\'97three\'97four and they hit it at nearly three beats a second. Within twelve bars, the gates were shaking to their hinges. The mansion\'92s security system, programmed to detect conventional threats\'97broken glass, unusual heat, unauthorised heartbeats and several dozen varieties of suspicious footwear\'97but had no defences against upright basses and weaponised rockabilly. Alarms stuttered, sensors failed, and somewhere in the guest house, a wine cellar\'92s climate control system wept.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93Go, go, go!\'94 A Tulsa ordered.\
They almost 
\f3\i went, went, went!
\f1\i0  but had to return their guitars to their cases first. Then most of them  surged up the driveway like a sequinned jailhouse break, while half a dozen Tulsas guarded the gate.\
Chanta called Johnny. \'93We\'92re in. Where are the Gyges discs?\'94\
Johnny paused.\
\'93Come on, Johnny. We\'92re here.\'94\
\'93Stasis units.\'94\
\'93What?\'94\
\'93They drive stasis units.\'94\
Chanta made a sound that tried to be a swear word but came out somewhere between a cough and a gargle. \'93Are you crazy? No one taxing taxes with Fridge Force.\'94\
\'93Relax,\'94 Johnny said, and it sounded to Chanta like he was whispering. \'93We\'92ve got Fridge Force personnel on the project.\'94\
\'93Sarah\'92s project.\'94\
\'93Well, it\'92s my project, technically, but yes.\'94\
\'93And she\'92s on board with this.\'94\
\'93She supports my leadership.\'94\
\'93And she knows where to find them.\'94\
\'93Tax! How do we get the discs out?\'94\
\'93I\'92ll walk you through it. There\'92s one in every stasis unit\'85 any cupboard, closet, even store rooms. The machinery is the same.\'94\
Chanta started with the kitchen; there was a large walk-in closet at the back near the appliance nook. Johnny talked Chanta through it. He located the panel marked 
\fs18 NO SERVICEABLE PARTS INSIDE
\fs22  and popped it out; he located the bulbous green component which bore a sign, 
\fs18 WARNING: TAMPERING WITH STASIS TECHNOLOGY INVALIDATES THE WARRANTY OF YOUR LIFE
\f3\i .
\f1\i0  
\fs22 He unbolted the green component from the rest of the gadgetry. Johnny talked him through removing the disc from it.\
As the disc glimmered in his hand, Chanta held his breath and listened. He expected alarms or something. None came.
\fs18 \

\fs22 Two teams went through the mansion to repeat the procedure. Chanta grabbed a couple of bananas and a jar of peanut butter, and sat in the family room. The first banana broke off in the jar. Before he knew it, Chanta was finger-deep in peanut butter.\
The first team returned while Chanta was washing his hands in the kitchen sink. Chanta examined the two discs. They were genuine, and a little scary; Chanta had a flashing vision of garlic sauce all over the windscreen of his trashed van. \'93Excellent work. Where\'92s the other team?\'94\
\'93Just finishing up,\'94 said the team leader.\
\'93Finishing up what?\'94 Chanta asked. \'93We\'92ve got what we came for.\'94\
The second team returned.\
They had secured four more discs.\
\'93That\'92s twice as many as we needed,\'94 Chanta complained.\
\'93Three for you, three for the High Elvis,\'94 the second team leader said. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

